> ---
> 
> ## The key classification: `effective_measure_type`
> 
> I would make this the central variable in your analysis.
> 
> | Code | Meaning | What varies in growth? |
> |---|---|---|
> | `national_real` | Real GDP/GDPpc in national prices, perhaps still in local currency | Domestic volume growth; no exchange-rate or PPP movement |
> | `fixed_PPP_real` | National real GDP/GDPpc expressed using a PPP conversion fixed in one reference year | Domestic volume growth; PPP only changes level/units, not growth |
> | `chained_PPP_real` | PPP-based chained real GDP/GDPpc series, such as the relevant PWT-style chain series | Domestic growth plus effects of chained international relative-price treatment |
> | `annual_PPP` | Current-price GDP converted using a contemporaneous PPP each year | Domestic nominal changes and time-varying PPP changes |
> | `fixed_MER_real` | National real GDP expressed with a fixed-year market exchange rate | Domestic volume growth; MER only changes level/units, not growth |
> | `annual_MER` | Current-price GDP converted at the contemporaneous market exchange rate | Domestic nominal changes plus exchange-rate changes |
> | `US_deflated_MER` | Convert to USD at annual MER, then deflate using US prices | Exchange-rate changes plus US-price deflation |
> | `other` | Anything not cleanly fitting above | Document briefly |
> 
> For the question “do alternative GDP datasets affect the results?”, this type is likely more useful than a fully detailed methodology taxonomy.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## PPP timing, separately
> 
> Keep `PPP_treatment` as a check on the main classification:
> 
> | Entry | Meaning |
> |---|---|
> | `none` | No PPP conversion in the published measure |
> | `fixed` | One PPP benchmark/reference-year conversion is applied throughout |
> | `annual` | A country-year-specific PPP factor is applied each year |
> | `chained` | PPP/international-price comparisons enter through chain-linking |
> | `other/unknown` | Cannot be cleanly assigned |
> 
> This makes the practical distinction clear:
> 
> - **Fixed PPP**: should not alter within-country growth rates relative to the underlying national-real series, apart from revisions, splices, or differing population data.
> - **Annual PPP**: can alter measured growth because PPP factors change over time.
> - **Chained PPP**: can alter measured growth, though not as simply as “annual PPP conversion.”
> - **No PPP**: may still be a sound domestic-growth series; it is just not PPP-level comparable.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Example rows
> 
> | collection_id | source_version | series | concept | effective_measure_type | PPP_treatment | price_basis | reference_year |
> |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
> | `PWT62_RGDPCH` | PWT 6.2 | `RGDPCH`, real GDPpc chain series | GDPpc | `chained_PPP_real` | `chained` | real | `chain` |
> | `WDI_GDPPC_PPP_CONSTANT` | WDI vintage X | GDP per capita, constant Int$ | GDPpc | likely `fixed_PPP_real`* | `fixed`* | real | e.g. `2017` |
